 (3623,3657,'PERFORMANCE MONITORING',evidence('CAMPAIGN3_PERFORMANCE_QUALIFICATION.md'),'Four models22 public runs198 prefixes connect own admitted failure to later route switch under fixed goal and known availability. Two consecutive admitted failures within current visit trigger switch; success resets,missing neither increments nor resets. VisitStartedAt prevents old failures reused on return. Baseline actually attempts/executes B4 after A failures; success does not prove B superiority because apparatus removes blocker4 and either route could succeed. OutcomeBlind/AnyFailure/TruthOracle remain; false failures can trigger unnecessary switch,hidden obstruction versus competence remains observationally equal. Desired-state attainment separately retires goal; performance success alone cannot fulfill. Monitoring40 uses prior140,plan90/attempt100/execution110 are actual consumers with no new Decision/intent claim. No optimal threshold,causal diagnosis or learned relative efficacy.'),
